The legal risks associated with tracking people without their consent include privacy violations, invasion of their right to security, and potentially damaging their reputation. It is important to clearly state in your data collection policy that information will be collected for intended purposes and with the consent of all parties involved. Additionally, ensure that the methods used for collecting the data are secure and not accessible by unauthorized parties. Proper encryption techniques should also be used to protect personal identifiers that could lead back to an individual, such as names or addresses. If possible, users should also be provided an opt-out option so they can prevent any additional tracking after initially providing consent.
